    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0977" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg967"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3–2146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in China </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-21T14:00:00-05:00">March 21, 1946—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>505. Board Directors Eximbank on Mar 20, 1946 approved renewal undisbursed
                    balance 50 Million Dollar loan to Central Bank of China <pb facs="0978" n="968"
                        xml:id="pg968"/> under agreement dated Feb. 4, 1941.<anchor n="98"
                        xml:id="d688-f1"/> Undisbursed balance of $9,204,706.78 renewed for period
                    12 months ending Dec. 31, 1946.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d688-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d688-f1" n="98" xml:id="d688-f1-content">
                <p>Further details of this agreement are found in a note from the Chinese
                    Ambassador, January 6, 1941, <ref target="frus1941v05#pg_593">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, p. 593</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d688-f2" n="99" xml:id="d688-f2-content">
                <p>In his note of March 29 the Chinese Ambassador informed the Secretary of State
                    that his Government had authorized extension of this agreement to December 31,
                    1946 (893.51/3–2946).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
